I'll finalize the design first, not directly change the code.

I suggest we follow this plan:

1. Add a unified sandhi pass at runtime: change the handling of 一/不/third-tone sandhi from "baked into entries" to "whole-sentence syllable-level processing".
2. The generator only keeps basic pronunciations and neutral tones, no longer hardcodes 一/不 tone sandhi in entries.
3. Gradually converge the OOV fallback to a single-character lexicon, with pinyin_converter as the last resort.

Why this approach:

- Modifying only the generator would continue to be overridden by long words, still whack-a-mole.
- Unified runtime processing can cover issues like 一下 / 检查一下 / 很好 / 请你 / 为你 in one go.
- After converging fallback sources, the pronunciation source becomes more consistent, making future audits easier.

If you agree, I'll implement this plan.
